# Tests for -trace-intern-table, which writes the SpeedyString table
# when bsc exits: every interned spelling with its id, one
# "id<TAB>spelling" line per entry in id order.  Ids compare by intern
# id, so a change that moves the first forcing of a string can change
# Map and Set orders and the generated names with them; two compiles
# whose tables are identical interned the same strings in the same
# order.  The dump goes to the file named by BSC_INTERN_DUMP, or without
# it next to the .bo as <package>.intern.tsv.  Two compiles of the same
# source must leave identical tables, and the table starts at id 0.
#
# The compiles run with -v, which prints "types OK" for every internal
# check that ran: four package-level checks (iPCheck after internal,
# fixup, isimpdicts and isimplify) and, per synthesized module, the
# module check after expanded, six more after the post-expansion passes
# (iMCheck after Fmt inline, inline, transform, splitIf, lift and
# transform) and the ASyntax checks; two modules here, 46 in all.

erase ICheck.bo
compile_backend_pass ICheck.bs {-trace-intern-table -v}
find_n_strings ICheck.bs.bsc-out {types OK} 46
find_regexp ICheck.intern.tsv {^0\t"}
move ICheck.intern.tsv ICheck.checked.intern.tsv
move ICheck.bo ICheck.checked.bo
move mkCounter.v mkCounter.checked.v
move sysICheck.v sysICheck.checked.v

erase ICheck.bo
set ::env(BSC_INTERN_DUMP) "ICheck.env.intern.tsv"
compile_backend_pass ICheck.bs {-trace-intern-table -v}
unset ::env(BSC_INTERN_DUMP)
compare_file ICheck.env.intern.tsv ICheck.checked.intern.tsv

# -hack-no-icheck-package makes the four package-level checks no-ops and
# -hack-no-icheck-passes the six post-expansion module checks; the check
# after expanded and the ASyntax checks still run, so sixteen "types OK"
# lines fewer.  A check is a pure re-typing whose Bool only feeds an
# internal error, but it is also the first consumer of the pass's lazy
# result, so skipping it is admissible only if the dump that follows
# forces the same thunks and no string is first interned in a different
# order: the .bo, both generated Verilog files and the intern table
# must be identical to the checked compile's.
erase ICheck.bo
compile_backend_pass ICheck.bs {-trace-intern-table -hack-no-icheck-package -hack-no-icheck-passes -v}
find_n_strings ICheck.bs.bsc-out {types OK} 30
compare_file ICheck.bo ICheck.checked.bo
compare_file mkCounter.v mkCounter.checked.v
compare_file sysICheck.v sysICheck.checked.v
compare_file ICheck.intern.tsv ICheck.checked.intern.tsv
